## GAME TYPES:
- Pop the Balloon (lesson 1)
- Each letter of a word is a balloon (Ex: S U M A K A Y)
- Pop the U and M balloons from S U M A K A Y. Keep S A K A Y as the root word.
- Whack-a-Mole (lesson 2)
- Mole with associated word appears, need to select among the 4 types of kayarian before
it goes back under. Score is based on how many you can whack, the more whack the

higher the score. So the goal is neverending since magagad man ka nga mabeat imong
previous score
- Supply the Tiles (lesson 3)
- Given a set of panlapi (may be unlapi, hulapi, gitlapi, or kabilaan + 1 empty tile (since
user has to figure out which of the 4 panlapi is needed based on the sentence)) supply
the needed tiles
- Use dnd.kit for this
- Match the cards (lesson 4)
- given multiple cards (at most 20) match them to create new words
Ex: word1 = bahay, word2 = kubo => match = bahay-kubo
## 5. Ticket Stub Dispenser (lesson 5)
- A ticket printer can output two full matching tickets (full reduplication) or one full ticket
plus a torn partial stub showing just the first letters (partial). Player reads the sentence
and pulls the correct print lever.
## 6. Claw Machine (lesson 6)
- Choose which doll is the “pokus ng pandiwa” based on the sentence
## 7. Fortune Predict (lesson 7)
- A root enters the fortune machine with pang-; predict the transformed output before the
card prints.


